// ─── What they have agreed to ───────────────────────────────────────────────

// ── Pay ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every leg of a paystub is a constant while salary and elections are, so it lives in the contract and a
// paystub is `15 job-lumen`. (The v4 sketch restates the same six legs 24 times a year.)
// ✗ 02a3: nothing derives the withholding legs from the salary and the W-4. A raise, a move or a new election
// restates all of them by hand, which is what the statements on 2026-08-16 and 2026-10-16 below do.

contract job-lumen with lumen                      // Priya: 138,000 a year
  5_750 USD twice monthly on 15, last into me-checking
  until 2026-08-31
  -> retirement-lumen 6%                              // ▸ pre-tax deferral
  -> blue-shield 210.00 USD #premium                  // ▸ pre-tax (§125)
  -> irs 785.30 USD                                   // ▸ federal tax paid for the year of the paycheck
  -> ftb 341.20 USD
  -> ssa 439.88 USD                                   // ▸ Social Security and Medicare: 7.65%
  -> edd 74.75 USD                                    // ▸ California SDI
  -> match 50% of retirement-lumen up to 6%           // ▸ Lumen adds 172.50 to each 345.00

contract job-harbor with harbor-labs               // Priya: 148,000 a year, from 2026-09-08
  6_166.67 USD twice monthly on 15, last into joint-checking
  from 2026-09-08
  -> retirement-harbor 6%
  -> blue-shield 240.00 USD #premium
  -> irs 862.40 USD
  -> dtf 318.70 USD                                   // ▸ New York State
  -> nyc-dof 173.15 USD                               // ▸ New York City resident tax
  -> ssa 471.75 USD
  -> ny-pfl 23.93 USD
  -> match 100% of retirement-harbor up to 3%
  // ✗ 02a4: the first paycheck, 09-15, covers 09-08 to 09-15 only. No way to say "prorated by the days worked";
  // it is written with its amount below (journal/2026/09.ax).

contract job-jamie with pinnacle                   // Jamie: 105,600 a year
  4_400 USD twice monthly on 15, last into jamie-checking
  -> retirement-jamie 5%
  -> blue-shield 165.00 USD #premium
  -> hsa 250.00 USD                                   // ▸ pre-tax, into the HSA
  -> irs 402.60 USD
  -> ftb 176.10 USD
  -> ssa 336.60 USD
  -> edd 57.20 USD
  -> match 100% of retirement-jamie up to 3%

/// Pinnacle puts a fixed 100 USD a month into Jamie's HSA. Its own contract: `match` is a percentage of a
/// deferral and this is not one.
contract hsa-employer with pinnacle
  100 USD monthly on last into hsa #hsa-contribution

// The move changes which authorities are paid and how much, on the paycheck after 08-15.
// ✗ 02a7: a terms statement with legs. §5 says a statement "with an amount and a cadence restates the terms; what
// it leaves out carries over", and gives legs only to an occurrence ("replace the template's legs of the same
// end"). To drop a leg I write it `empty`; to add one I write it. Neither is in §5.
2026-08-16 job-jamie 4_400 USD twice monthly
  ftb empty
  edd empty
  dtf 190.40 USD
  nyc-dof 108.90 USD
  ny-pfl 17.06 USD
2026-10-16 job-jamie 4_400 USD twice monthly       // the baby: 500 USD a paycheck into the dependent-care FSA
  dcfsa 500.00 USD                                 // ✗ 02a1: until 2026-12-31: five paychecks make the 2,500 USD election

// ── The house ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Priya's 5/1 ARM: 520,000 USD at 2.875%, first payment 2021-03-01. It resets on the fifth anniversary.
contract mortgage with rocket
  loan 520_000 USD on 2021-01-15 at 2.875% over 30y for home
  monthly on 1 from me-checking
  escrow 675 USD into escrow                       // property tax and insurance
  until 2026-05-20                                 // paid off by the refinance

// The lender's notice arrived in December: 2/2/5 caps, so the reset is 2 points above 2.875%.
// ▸ 2,157.44 becomes 2,662.95 on the remaining 461,252.48 over 300 months.
2026-03-01 mortgage at 4.875%
2026-03-01 mortgage escrow 702.00 USD              // the annual escrow analysis, same notice

/// The refinance on 2026-05-20: 30 years fixed at 5.625%, with 20,000 USD taken out. The first payment is
/// 07-01: nothing is due in June.
contract mortgage-2 with newrez
  loan 480_039.99 USD on 2026-05-20 at 5.625% over 30y for home     // ✗ 02a5: `for home` is true of 460,039.99 of it
  monthly on 1 from joint-checking
  escrow 702.00 USD into escrow2
  from 2026-07-01

contract property-tax with alameda-county
  about 3_512.00 USD yearly on 04-10, 12-10 from escrow #property-tax of home    // ✎ 02b4: as 01's est-me, a list of dates
  covers 6m                                        // ✎ 02b4': each installment is for the half-year that ends on it

// ── The car ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

contract car-loan with sf-fcu
  loan 29_046.25 USD on 2026-02-14 at 5.9% over 60m for car2
  monthly on 14 from me-checking
  from 2026-03-14

contract auto-ca with state-farm
  940 USD every 6m on 03-01 from me-checking #insurance
  covers 6m
  until 2026-08-31
contract auto-ny with state-farm
  1_310 USD every 6m on 09-01 from joint-checking #insurance
  covers 6m
  from 2026-09-01

// ── Living ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

contract electricity-ca with pge
  about 148.00 USD monthly on 12 from me-checking #utilities
2026-09-12 electricity-ca about 62 USD monthly      // the house is empty from September
contract electricity-ny with coned
  about 118.00 USD monthly on 14 from joint-checking #utilities
  from 2026-09-14

/// The apartment, from the day they move in. Rent is 4,850 USD; the deposit is a month's rent.
/// ? 02c3: §5's `deposit` is "a claim the party holds, and money held for it". For a tenant the deposit is money
/// *we* paid, held by them: the same word, the opposite direction, and nothing says which one this is.
contract nyc-lease with west-84th
  4_850 USD monthly on 1 from joint-checking #rent
  deposit 4_850 USD
  from 2026-08-15
  // ✗ 02a4: 08-15 to 08-31 is 17 of 31 days: 2,659.68. Written as an amount on the occurrence.

contract daycare with little-oaks
  2_300 USD monthly on 1 from joint-visa #childcare
  from 2026-11-10                                  // ✗ 02a4: the first month is 21 of 30 days

contract 529-noa-monthly with ny-529
  250 USD monthly on 5 from joint-checking into 529-noa
  from 2026-11-05

// When they marry the household's bills move to the joint account. One statement each.
// ✗ 02a6: an account is replaced by another for every contract that names it. There is no "moves to".
2026-06-13 auto-ca from joint-checking
2026-06-13 electricity-ca from joint-checking
2026-06-13 car-loan from joint-checking
